go 1.26.4

// go-radx is two modules: the library at the repository root and the radx CLI in its own
// module (cmd/radx) so library consumers do not inherit the CLI's dependency graph. This
// workspace composes both so editor tooling and cross-module commands resolve them as one
// tree, with the CLI building against the in-tree library rather than a published version.
// It does not widen the `./...` pattern: that pattern stops at the nested cmd/radx module
// boundary, so `go build ./...` / `go test ./...` from the root still cover the root module
// only. The cmd-radx CI job sets GOWORK=off to build cmd/radx against its own go.mod/go.sum.
use (
	.
	./cmd/radx
)
